Administrative checks after a forest cohort registration
========================================================

Purpose and roles
-----------------

This package contains a new metadata checker for the existing, immutable
755a448d cohort registrar. It replaces repetition in the administrative
check, not the mathematical proofs or their independent reviews. Its entry
has not been executed. All request and decision examples are false.

Root must read and own the complete checker, this protocol, its exact Source
manifest and a distinct positive Source peer before granting one execution.
The Source author is /root/dependency_audit. The Source peer must be neither
the author, Root nor /root/readback_review. Root executes the admitted code
under a genuine supervisor and owns the fresh positive decision. The result
states that role separation explicitly; it does not call Root an independent
mathematical reviewer or fabricate a scientific SDK.

The checker reads an already completed registrar invocation, its genuine
SDK/raw API records, its guard, and the saved before and after images. It
launches no process, runs no writer, evaluates no scientific predicate and
changes no canonical file. Its only output is a fresh private result file.
Existing scientific, control, roster, model and mathematical premises remain
imports of the accepted batch and aggregate reviews. Their full historical
ancestry is not recursively reopened.

Accepted input contract
