Payload handling
----------------

The standalone byte parser splits JSON object/array spans without decoding
Original values. Only named metadata fields and explicitly payload-free
records are decoded. A recursive metadata gate rejects parent, parents,
records, covers, cache_entries, representatives, next_parent_forests,
forest, forests, matrices, permutations, transporter, transporters and
witness fields before decoding a candidate metadata object. Cache containers
are handled through the dedicated lexical branch rather than that gate.
No scientific certificate, pairing payload, roster array, matrix, group word,
permutation or graph is decoded or evaluated. Code and certificates from
accepted upstream work are not imported as executable modules.

